---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  heading="Cookie Policy"
  description="Cookie Policy for gokhan.vc. Only strictly-necessary Cloudflare security cookies are used — no advertising, analytics, or tracking, and no consent banner required."
  lastUpdated="22 June 2026"
>
  <div class="note">
    <p>
      gokhan.vc uses <strong
        >no advertising, analytics, profiling, or cross-site tracking cookies</strong
      >, embeds no third-party marketing pixels, and loads no consent-management platform. The only
      cookies that may be set are <strong>strictly necessary security cookies</strong> placed by our infrastructure
      provider, Cloudflare, to protect the site against bots and abuse and to deliver content.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Why there is no consent banner</h2>
  <p>
    Under Article 5(3) of the ePrivacy Directive (2002/58/EC) and its national transpositions — UK
    PECR reg. 6(4), Germany’s TDDDG §25(2), and France via the CNIL —
    <strong>strictly necessary cookies are exempt from prior consent</strong>. Because the site sets
    only such cookies and no non-essential storage, GDPR’s consent machinery is not triggered. Our
    obligation is <strong>transparency</strong>, met by this page — not a consent prompt. Adding a
    banner would itself introduce unnecessary storage, so we deliberately do not.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies that may be set</h2>
  <div class="cookie-table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Cookie</th>
          <th>Set by</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
          <th>Duration</th>
          <th>Type / legal basis</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>__cf_bm</code></td>
          <td>Cloudflare</td>
          <td>
            Bot management — distinguishes humans from automated traffic to protect the site. Not
            used for advertising or cross-site tracking.
          </td>
          <td>~30 min (rolling)</td>
          <td>
            Strictly necessary — exempt from consent (ePrivacy Art 5(3)); security processing under
            GDPR Art 6(1)(f)
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>cf_clearance</code></td>
          <td>Cloudflare</td>
          <td>
            Stores the result of a security challenge so a verified visitor is not re-challenged on
            every request.
          </td>
          <td>~30 min</td>
          <td>Strictly necessary — exempt from consent; GDPR Art 6(1)(f)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>__cflb</code> / <code>cf_use_ob</code></td>
          <td>Cloudflare</td>
          <td>Session routing for load balancing (may not appear on this site).</td>
          <td>Session / short-lived</td>
          <td>Strictly necessary — exempt from consent</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <p>
    We set <strong>no first-party cookies</strong>. We do not sell or share any data derived from
    these cookies, and we do not use them for advertising, profiling, or targeted advertising
    (CCPA/CPRA).
  </p>

  <h2>Managing cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Because these cookies are strictly necessary, blocking them in your browser may break security
    challenges and prevent the site from loading. You can still delete them at any time via your
    browser settings. For how Cloudflare processes request data, see Cloudflare’s cookie
    documentation and privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about cookies or privacy: <a href="mailto:contact@gokhan.vc">contact@gokhan.vc</a>.
    See also our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
